    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureAppleUsbmux">The Apple USB pairing service is not ready. Install or repair Apple Devices/iTunes support in the driver manager, connect and unlock the iPhone, then try again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureNotTrusted">This iPhone has not trusted the current Windows account. Keep the phone unlocked, reconnect the cable, and tap “Trust” on the phone.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureDeviceLocked">The iPhone is locked. Unlock it, confirm any Trust or passcode prompt, then start control again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureDeveloperMode">Developer Mode is off. Turn it on under Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Developer Mode, restart the device and retry.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureImageRequired">The device has not mounted the Personalized Developer Disk Image. Mount the official Xcode image matching the device system, then try again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureImageDownload">The developer image download failed or timed out. Check the GitHub network connection, or provide an official local image through IPHONE_MIRROR_DDI_DIR.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureImageCache">Couldn't save the developer image. Check free space and write access to your user folder, then retry.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureImageRateLimited">GitHub has temporarily rate limited developer image downloads. Please retry later.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureImageIntegrity">Developer image verification failed. The download may be incomplete or damaged. Check the network or use another image source, then retry.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureImageIncompatible">The developer image doesn't match this device. Update to the latest package and retry.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureImageTss">Apple image personalization failed or returned an invalid response. Check the network and proxy settings and retry. Retain the diagnostic log if it persists.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureImageRemount">The old Personalized Developer Disk Image could not be refreshed. Close Xcode or other tools using the device, restart the iPhone, and try again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureImageMount">The device couldn't mount the developer image. Unlock and reconnect it, close other developer tools, then retry.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureUnsupportedIos">The device rejected touch control (9021). Restart the iPhone and retry; if it still fails, use Bluetooth control.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureTouchSurface">A CoreDevice session was established, but the developer image did not publish the mainTouchscreen (257) touch surface. Restart the iPhone and try again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureWirelessPairingRequired">Wireless control isn't paired yet. Start wired control once over USB, then try wireless again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureWirelessNotDiscoverable">The iPhone wireless CoreDevice service was not found. Keep the iPhone unlocked on the same local network and allow Windows firewall discovery.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureWirelessPairingFailed">Wireless CoreDevice pairing or tunnel setup failed. Connect by USB once and complete initialization, then confirm the iPhone is unlocked and the network does not isolate clients.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureWirelessDiscoveryUnavailable">Couldn't search for wireless devices. Check the network adapter, the firewall and UDP port 5353, then retry.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureWirelessAddressResolution">Found the iPhone but no usable address. Keep it unlocked on the same network and check router client isolation or mDNS (UDP 5353).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureGateUnavailable">The device did not confirm that CoreDevice touch authentication is enabled. Reverse control was not started to prevent silent input loss.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureDeviceConnectionTimeout">Connecting to the device timed out. Keep the iPhone unlocked, reconnect the USB cable and confirm that this computer is trusted, then retry.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureTouchService">The device has not provided the touch-control service. Keep it unlocked and trusted, then try again; otherwise use Bluetooth or wireless control.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureDeviceNotFound">No network pairing found. Connect by cable once and turn on “Sync with this iPhone over Wi-Fi” in Apple Devices or iTunes, then retry.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureWiredDeviceNotFound">No control channel over USB. Stop mirroring first, or replug the cable, unlock the iPhone, confirm Trust and retry.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureMux">The Apple USB service disconnected during the device handshake. Keep the device unlocked and trusted, reconnect the cable, and try again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureNoDetails">The USB touch bridge provided no error details. Confirm the device is connected by USB and trusted.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="UsbControlFailureUnknown">Reverse control could not start for an unidentified reason. Reconnect the device and retry. If it persists, submit the diagnostic log.</system:String>
